  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Rystiggo (rozanolixizumab-noli) Criteria Version 1; Original 07/25/2024; Accepted 09/20/2024; Effective 11/1/2024.",
    "Approval criteria 1-8 and denial exclusions are encoded as attestations. Immunosuppressive examples include corticosteroids, azathioprine and mycophenolate. The AChR and MuSK treatment-history branches are when-gated; required PE, IVIG or plasmapheresis in addition to maintenance therapy qualifies for either branch.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval 6 weeks. Reauthorization up to 6 months requires at least a 1 point improvement in MG-ADL total score, ongoing treatment needed for new or worsening disease activity despite initial positive response, no treatment limiting adverse events, and at least 63 days since completion of the previous treatment cycle.",
    "Cautions (notes only): aseptic meningitis has been reported; monitor for signs/symptoms during treatment. Live or live-attenuated vaccines are not recommended during treatment due to transient IgG reduction. Common adverse reactions include headache, infections, diarrhea, pyrexia, hypersensitivity reactions and nausea.",
    "Quantity/dosing (manual review): follow labeling and the archived policy limits of 24 ml (12 2 ml vials) per 28 days; 36 ml (18 2 ml vials) per 63 days. PDF states maximum recommended dosage 840 mg once weekly for six weeks and subsequent cycles no sooner than 63 days after completion of the previous cycle. The PDF parenthetical says \"3 2mg vials\", inconsistent with its 2 ml vial units; verify against labeling. HCPCS J9333. max_units is null because multiple windows and dosing require manual review.",
    "Remains partial: evidence documentation, cautions, duration, reauthorization, quantity and dosing require manual review. PDL status unknown."
  ],
